!
! A wind speed in tenths of a metre a second as tenths of a kilometre an
! hour (weatherglass_model.h WG1), in Trebago: 1 m/s is 3.6 km/h, so
! wind * 36 / 10 = wind * 18 / 5, an exact reduced rational, never rounded
! (1 is 18/5, 3.6 tenths). The domain is 0 .. 2000 tenths (200 m/s, past
! any gust measured): ok is 1 inside it and 0 outside, and the answer is
! divided by it, so a negative or faster wind is a division by zero,
! refused, where wind.kron answers: held.
trebago wind
  in  wind(n)
  out kmh(n)
  var ok(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, wind(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, 2001 - wind(i)))
  kmh(i) = wind(i) * 18 / 5 / ok(i)
end
